   "note": "the figure of chapter 57, «the long alidade», drawn by hand in the print: an upright line (the ruler ز ح) from a little above the ring at ز down through the ring at ط to a dot in the oblong at its foot, in which ح stands; at ز a thick ring with a disc in its middle, at ط a smaller ring with a disc; from ز a line sloping down to the right (the ruler ز ل) to the point ل on the third ruler, with two small sights standing on its right side, each an oblong with a slit; from the ring at ط a line rising to the right (the ruler ط م) to its end at م, with thirty steps standing square on its upper side from ط to ك, every fifth one taller; the letters ز, ط, ل, ك, م beside their points, ا and د outside the upper corners of the oblong and ب and ج under it. Measured on the master scan at 1200 dpi: the upright line from the middles of its stroke across it at twenty heights (it is not quite straight), the rings from their edges on rays that avoid the lines, the sloping line and the ruler by straight fits to the middle of their strokes, every step from the ink beside the ruler (its place, thickness and height), the sights from their outer form and their slits in the frame of the sloping line (drawn as two walls and a cover; the print rounds their corners), the oblong from fits to its four sides, the dot from its edge. The labels are set in the type of the edition at the centres of their printed ink"
  }
